# Frontend search field consistency

When adding or changing a **customer/list search** (filter by name, phone, or similar):

1. **Reuse global classes** from `frontend/src/styles.css`: `.search-container` > `.search-input-wrapper`, `.search-icon`, `.search-input-modern`, `.btn-clear-search`, and optional `.search-suggestions` / `.suggestion-item` (same as Outstanding Due).
2. **Matching rules**: For name + phone filtering, mirror Outstanding Due `filterCardsByState` / `updateSearchSuggestions` (lowercase name `includes`, digits-only phone with `phone.includes(normalizedQuery) || normalizedQuery.includes(phone)`).
3. **Placeholder**: Prefer `Search by customer name or phone...` unless the domain truly differs.
4. **Behaviour**: Prefer an explicit filtered array refreshed on `(input)` / focus (not only a template getter) so the list updates reliably with `ngModel`.
5. Do not add one-off search styles on feature pages; extend `styles.css` when sharing new pieces.

References: `outstanding-due.component.ts` (`filterCardsByState`, `updateSearchSuggestions`), `whatsapp-outreach` recipient search.
